{"data": {"id": "476818a67d104daa50196169980ddf6abbb9d01fe90ad16777df59197d8d9a89", "lineage": "476818a67d104daa50196169980ddf6abbb9d01fe90ad16777df59197d8d9a89", "origin": "sample:3", "parent": null, "source": "def count_kagamimochis(N, A):\n    # Sort the list of mochis in ascending order\n    A.sort()\n    \n    # Initialize a dictionary to store the frequency of each size of mochi\n    freq = {}\n    \n    # Count the frequency of each size of mochi\n    for size in A:\n        if size in freq:\n            freq[size] += 1\n        else:\n            freq[size] = 1\n    \n    # Calculate the number of different kinds of kagamimochi\n    num_kagamimochis = 0\n    \n    # Iterate over each pair of mochis\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            # Check if the current pair can form a kagamimochi\n            if A[i] <= A[j] / 2:\n                # Add the frequency of the smaller size to the total number of kagamimochis\n                num_kagamimochis += min(freq[A[i]], freq[A[j]])\n    \n    return num_kagamimochis\n\n# Read input\nN = int(input())\nA = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Print the result\nprint(count_kagamimochis(N, A))"}, "kind": "candidate", "prev": "b8b939f4e2b77f37daad905a24651d07122277851ace9e1406d7b75942c594ff", "seq": 20}
